A <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-air/">MacBook Air</a> with a new look could launch in late 2027 or 2028, <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> said in <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-25/power-on-podcast-mark-answers-listener-questions-video?srnd=phx-poweronpodcast">the latest episode</a> of his Power On podcast. Apple plans to refresh the &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj; with M6 chips in early 2027 alongside the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-neo/">MacBook Neo</a> 2, but that update won't include a new design.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/m5-macbook-air-pink.jpeg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1078957" /><br/>
A more extensive overhaul could follow later in 2027 or in 2028, and the &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj; could get an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> display at that time.<br/>
<blockquote>MacBook Air is Apple's most popular computer, and they need to keep it very fresh. And so my anticipation is 2027, 2028 is when we're going to get the big MacBook Air overhaul. And I think OLED will be part of that conversation.</blockquote><br/>
Apple last overhauled the &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj;'s design in 2022, eliminating the prior wedge shape for a more uniform MacBook Pro-style chassis. The machine adopted a brighter Liquid Retina display with a notch for the camera, and a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/magsafe/">MagSafe</a> charging port. In 2023, Apple added a 15-inch model, but since then, we've only gotten minor updates.<br/>
<br/>
Apple just added &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> with the launch of the 2026 PROLED models, so it's not clear whether the high-end display will trickle down to the &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj; that quickly. In <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/02/oled-macbook-air-expected-in-2028/">prior reports</a>, Gurman has leaned more toward the 2028 timeline than late 2027.<br/>
<br/>
